# Byte fidelity everywhere: what is committed is what checks out, on
# every platform. Git's working-tree conversion (Windows autocrlf)
# rewrote every text file to CRLF on the Windows runners, breaking the
# pinned upstream snapshot hashes and the corpus patch markers — and a
# blanket eol=lf would corrupt the other direction: the vendored
# diagram-design files and their frozen upstream legitimately carry the
# CRLF their upstream author wrote. No conversion, ever, either way.
* -text
